# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Ondu Karaoke — frontend (build-time) environment
#
# Vite inlines these into the bundle at BUILD time, so they have to be set
# before `npm run build` (or as project env vars on your host).
#
# Leave everything empty for the default setup, where the Express backend
# serves the built frontend and the API from the same origin.
#
#   VITE_REALTIME=ws        → use the Cloudflare Workers WebSocket transport
#                             (the Worker serves the app itself — no other
#                              variable is needed)
#   VITE_BACKEND_URL=…      → Socket.IO origin (only for a split deployment
#                             where the Node backend lives somewhere else)
#   VITE_API_URL=…          → REST API origin (same)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# VITE_REALTIME=ws
# VITE_BACKEND_URL=https://ondu-karaoke-api.onrender.com
# VITE_API_URL=https://ondu-karaoke-api.onrender.com

# Optional: live cat/dog memes from GIPHY.
# Create a free *Web* key at https://developers.giphy.com/dashboard/ and
# restrict it to your app's domain (localhost for local dev). GIPHY requires
# browser-side search calls, so this key is public by design — never use a
# private/secret key here. Set it BEFORE building. Without it the bundled GIFs
# in client/public/gifs are used instead.
# VITE_GIPHY_API_KEY=your_domain_restricted_giphy_web_key
